{"name":"Thunder Grey","hex":"#57534c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"thunder","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The loud rumbling, cracking, or crashing sound caused by expansion of rapidly heated air around a lightning bolt.","A deep, rumbling noise resembling thunder."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To produce thunder; to sound, rattle, or roar, as a discharge of atmospheric electricity.","To make a noise like thunder."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thunder"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Thunder","blocks":[{"text":"Thunder is the sound caused by lightning. Depending upon the distance from and nature of the lightning, it can range from a long, low rumble to a sudden, loud crack. The sudden increase in temperature and hence pressure caused by the lightning produces rapid expansion of the air in the path of a lightning bolt. In turn, this expansion of air creates a sonic shock wave, often referred to as a \"thunderclap\" or \"peal of thunder\". The scientific study of thunder is known as brontology and the irrational fear (phobia) of thunder is called brontophobia."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thunder"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey"}],"images